      ":question/id": "83476731-0ea7-591d-b86a-90f71bae1c0a",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/problem": "Simplify.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\sin\\left(118^\\circ\\right)\\tan\\left(59^\\circ\\right)}{\\left(1+\\cos\\left(59^\\circ\\right)\\right)}\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Write $s=\\sin\\left(59^\\circ\\right)$ and $c=\\cos\\left(59^\\circ\\right)$. The **double-angle formula** gives $\\sin\\left(118^\\circ\\right)=2sc$.\n\n Also, $\\tan\\left(59^\\circ\\right)=\\frac{s}{c}$.\n\nRewrite the quotient ratio and cancel. Use $s^2+c^2=1$, factor the difference of squares, then cancel the matching binomial.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{2sc\\frac{s}{c}}{(1+c)} &=\\frac{2s^2}{(1+c)} \\\\ &=2\\frac{1-c^2}{(1+c)} \\\\ &=2\\frac{(1-c)(1+c)}{(1+c)} \\\\ &=2(1-c) \\\\ &=2\\left(1-\\cos\\left(59^\\circ\\right)\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAll cancellations use nonzero factors in the original expression.",
